From 6491619644df2b8b0224559bc522eb0cb6ff8d5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:13:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 105/105] vfio: nvtrace - GPU memory from the host side, large
 RPCs, firmware images

With NVTRACE_VRAM=1 a worker thread reads GPU memory itself:
- VRAM through a static BAR1 mapping (BAR1 page tables walked from
  GspStaticConfigInfo.bar1PdeBase, pread on the device fd) or through the
  BAR0 PRAMIN window (main-loop bottom half with the BQL held, BAR0 fully
  trapped, window register saved and restored), sysmem through the DMA
  address space;
- never before the WPR meta is known, never in [gspFwRsvdStart, fbSize),
  never again for a page that returned PRI error words;
- VRAM buffers named by RPCs (channel memdescs, LIST_FBMEM memory, vidmem
  display pushbuffers), every channel's instance block, its GMMU ver3 page
  tables, USERD GP_GET/GP_PUT, each new GPFIFO entry and the pushbuffer
  segment it points to (PUSHBUF records); optional VRAM sweep with
  per-page hashes (GPU_HASHES) and changed contents;
- triggered by doorbells, status messages, interrupts and display PUTs.

Large RPCs: CONTINUATION_RECORDs are appended before the RPC is followed.
Firmware and GSP-RM areas from guest memory, dumped once per change: the
GSP-RM ELF (radix3 page lists from the WPR meta), bootloader, signature,
FMC, every libos region, the GSP_ARGUMENTS_CACHED areas (profiler, sysmem
heap, state monitor, bindata); the crash report queue is watched. The
whole PCI config space is dumped at start and after resets.
---
